@page "/docs/components/vekdatagrid/presentation"
@layout DocumentationLayout

<PageTitle>VekDataGrid Presentation | Vek Components</PageTitle>

<div class="docs-page-layout">
    <article class="docs-article">
        <h1>VekDataGrid: Presentation</h1>
        <p class="docs-intro">Shape the grid around your product language with templates, culture-aware values, and accessible table semantics.</p>

        <section id="live-example" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="live-example-heading">
            <h2 id="live-example-heading">Live example</h2>
            <p>The toolbar and extra heading row are supplied by the page. Use the Edit action on a price cell to see the grid culture in its edit context.</p>
            @if (_products is null)
            {
                <p class="docs-loading" role="status">Loading sample products...</p>
            }
            else
            {
                <div class="docs-example-frame">
                    <VekDataGrid TItem="DemoProduct" Items="_products" PageSize="5"
                                 Culture="_culture" EditMode="VekDataGridEditMode.Cell"
                                 AriaLabel="Product inventory" data-testid="presentation-grid">
                        <ToolbarTemplate>
                            <span class="presentation-toolbar-label">Product inventory</span>
                            <span>@_products.Count products</span>
                        </ToolbarTemplate>
                        <HeaderTemplate>
                            <tr class="presentation-header-row">
                                <th colspan="3">DEMO INVENTORY · VALUES FORMATTED IN @_culture.Name</th>
                            </tr>
                        </HeaderTemplate>
                        <ChildContent>
                            <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Name" Title="Name" Key="Name">
                                <CellTemplate Context="product"><strong>@product.Name</strong></CellTemplate>
                            </PropertyColumn>
                            <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Category" Title="Category" Key="Category" />
                            <PropertyColumn Property="product => product.Price" Title="Price" Key="Price"
                                            Format="C2" Editable="true">
                                <EditTemplate Context="edit">
                                    <output aria-label="Edit culture">@edit.Item.Price.ToString("C2", edit.Culture)</output>
                                </EditTemplate>
                            </PropertyColumn>
                        </ChildContent>
                    </VekDataGrid>
                </div>
            }
        </section>

        <section id="code" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="code-heading">
            <h2 id="code-heading">Code</h2>
            <VekCodeViewMulti Tabs="_codeSamples" />
        </section>

        <section id="templates" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="templates-heading">
            <h2 id="templates-heading">Templates</h2>
            <p>Use <code>ToolbarTemplate</code> for content above the table and <code>HeaderTemplate</code> for extra semantic rows in the table heading. Column cells, row content, group headings, and footer content can also use templates.</p>
            <p>For a <code>RowTemplate</code>, render valid table cells for each item. It replaces the grid's default cell rendering for those rows while preserving the row's selection, click, and style behavior.</p>
        </section>

        <section id="culture-accessibility" class="docs-section-content" aria-labelledby="culture-accessibility-heading">
            <h2 id="culture-accessibility-heading">Culture and accessibility</h2>
            <p>Set <code>Culture</code> to control numeric and aggregate formatting. Edit templates receive that value through <code>VekDataGridEditContext.Culture</code>.</p>
            <p>Set <code>AriaLabel</code> to name the table for assistive technology. Unmatched attributes such as <code>data-testid</code> are applied directly to the native table. Built-in actions use labeled native controls that remain in the keyboard tab order.</p>
        </section>
    </article>

    <nav class="docs-toc" aria-label="On this page">
        <h2>On this page</h2>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/presentation#live-example">Live example</a>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/presentation#code">Code</a>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/presentation#templates">Templates</a>
        <a href="/docs/components/vekdatagrid/presentation#culture-accessibility">Culture and accessibility</a>
    </nav>
</div>
